PLAIN-SPEAK QUESTION

A52 found
a real timing lever.

Delayed response
helps the core
ride through temporary attacks.

But it also creates
a very specific mistake.

After a real reversal,
the cell can keep obeying
an old low-pressure message

even after
its current evidence says:

"my old commitment
is no longer supported."

A53 gives
current evidence
the final word.

While current evidence
still supports the commitment,

the cell may use
the three-turn-old response.

The instant
current evidence crosses against it,

the old message is discarded
and the cell reacts
to the present.

That is the final question
for the pulse benchmark:

CAN THE ORGANISM
KEEP USEFUL PHASE INERTIA

WITHOUT LETTING
STALE PHASE MEMORY
OVERRULE CURRENT REALITY?

After this answer,
we stop tuning the pulse world.

The next phase
is useful work.

